# Slice 334 (the author 2026-11-09: the part name is given explicitly whatever callable name exists): with the function
# name declared, `fn: name: k3; ...` still binds the part name by its head and creates k3; name stays the callable it is
# (name(2) 200, one call). Since M6 (slice 344) a colon Frame calls nothing, so the part `name: k3` is no call of name;
# since 4a (slice 345) the part is written by head only, `name := k3` giving no part (Codex
# CODEX-OPUS-345-4A-REPLY-20261110T041147Z-01 item 2) -- the receiver's form of the implemented stage, not the
# declaration of edition 4 (`k3: fn: ...`, M6 3).
fn: name (int: x) int (int: calls 0)
    calls: calls + 1
    return: x * 100
end: name
fn: name: k3; args: (int: a); return: int; body: (return: a + 2)
int: r1 k3(1)
int: r2 name(2)
int: c name\var\calls
